## Interface: 30300
## Title: GearScoreLite: Reborn
## Notes: Helps you quickly and easily judge a player's level of gear.
## Version: 4.1.0
## Author: Mirrikat45 & Gnomezilla [mod by Kappa]
## SavedVariables: GS_Settings, GS_Cache
## X-Conflicts: GearScore

# No OptionalDeps line, deliberately. It used to list ElvUI, ShadowedUnitFrames,
# VuhDo and WeakAuras, and that broke OmniCC for every WeakAuras icon.
#
# OptionalDeps does not merely document a soft dependency: it forces the listed
# addons to load BEFORE this one. GearScoreLite sorts ahead of OmniCC (G < O),
# so listing WeakAuras dragged WeakAuras ahead of OmniCC too. WeakAuras then
# registered PLAYER_LOGIN first, built its icon regions first, and each region
# copied Cooldown.SetCooldown into cooldown._SetCooldown, which it calls from
# then on instead of the metatable. OmniCC installs its hook by replacing that
# metatable entry on its own PLAYER_LOGIN, a moment too late: the copies were
# already taken, so no WeakAuras cooldown ever reached OmniCC again.
#
# Nothing here needs the ordering. Every reference to those addons is a runtime
# nil check (WeakAuras.ScanEvents in Announce, Focus.unit/.raidid in the tooltip
# path), which works whenever they happen to load. Re-adding the line reopens
# the bug for any addon that hooks a shared metatable at login.

informationLite.lua
GearScoreLite.lua